Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: Expose the disposer of an Own

Own<T>::disown() surrenders the object to a caller that already knows
the disposer, but gives no way to learn it. getDisposer() returns it, so
that an owner which keeps the object and its disposer apart -- a table
in memory of another protection class, say -- can take both out of an
Own and later dispose of the object the way the Own would have.

diff --git a/src/kj/memory.h b/src/kj/memory.h
--- a/src/kj/memory.h
+++ b/src/kj/memory.h
@@ -439,6 +439,10 @@
     ptr = nullptr;
     return ptrCopy;
   }
+
+  // The disposer the object will be disposed of with. Only valid if the Own is non-null.
+  inline const Disposer& getDisposer() const { return *disposer; }
+
 
 private:
   const Disposer* disposer;  // Only valid if ptr != nullptr.
